            "correct_answer": "The $4T$ signal has spacing $\\omega_0/4$, so its harmonic spectrum is denser.",
            "answer_explanation_blocks": [
              {
                "block_type": "paragraph",
                "text": "Use $\\omega_0 = 2\\pi/T$. Replacing $T$ by $4T$ makes the spacing one-fourth as large, so the harmonic lines move closer together.",
                "latex": "",
                "image_slot_id": ""
              },
              {
                "block_type": "display-math",
                "text": "",
                "latex": "\\omega_0' = \\frac{2\\pi}{4T} = \\frac{1}{4}\\omega_0",
